From 891d420c4ab5fed4f747f2646dad52115e914664 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Nichols A. Romero" <165712832+naromero77amd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:22:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [Release][Cherry-Pick] [AMD] Add initial GFX1250-strict
 Support (#11945) (#12134)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Cherry-pick of https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/11945 onto
`release/3.9.x` for https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/12121.

Source commit: `210fb9952a776ac63fce6ca24e69c7a925a09c05`

This was cherry-picked with `-x`.

Conflict resolution:
- #11945 updates two test cases introduced by #11707, which landed after
the release branch cut and is not present on `release/3.9.x`.
- Only those #11707-specific test hunks were omitted. All #11945
implementation changes and tests applicable to the release branch are
retained.

Validation:
- `python3 -m py_compile` on the changed Python files
- `git diff --check upstream/release/3.9.x..HEAD`
- IDE lint diagnostics: no errors

**Local testing** on an MI450 (`gfx1250`) with ROCm 10.1.0rc3 and
PyTorch 2.13.0. Built this PR's head (`62cfa305`) from source with the
release branch's pinned LLVM (`b010a18d`) and AMD codegen (`6bc4aaf6`).

Tests modified by this PR:
- Lit, all 8 modified files (each runs both its `gfx1250` and
`gfx1250-strict` RUN lines): 8/8 passed
- `third_party/amd/python/test/test_warp_pipeline_gfx9.py`: 3 passed
- `third_party/amd/python/test/test_gluon_cdna5.py`: 14,991 passed,
15,006 skipped, 1 failed (pre-existing, see below)
- `third_party/amd/python/test/test_gluon_cdna5.py` with
`TRITON_OVERRIDE_ARCH=gfx1250-strict`: 12,898 passed, 17,100 skipped, 0
failed
- `third_party/amd/python/examples/gluon/f16_gemm_cdna5.py`: 699 passed,
25 skipped, 16 failed (pre-existing, see below)
- `third_party/amd/python/examples/gluon/f16_fa_cdna5.py`: 11 passed
- `third_party/amd/python/examples/gluon/mxfp_fa_cdna5.py`: 90 passed

Also ran the full lit suite (303 passed, 2 plugin tests unsupported) and
the C++ unit tests (300/300 passed).

The strict run uses `gfx1250` hardware, which supports every strict
instruction, so it checks the strict compile paths and numerics but not
instruction legality on real `gfx1250-strict` hardware.

Pre-existing failures: all 17 also fail on unpatched `release/3.9.x`
(`aad2a60d`), and the generated instructions for these kernels are
identical with and without this PR.
- `test_runtime_scaled_upcast_fp8_non_broadcast_block16`: wrong results
(896/2048 elements) on every run, from the hardware Block16
`v_cvt_scale_pk8_bf16_fp8` path on this board
- `test_runtime_gemm_tdm_pipelined_multi_cta` (16 cases, all with 4×4
clusters): intermittent GPU memory access fault ("Page not present")

Co-authored-by: amirumoAMD <ameliamoorer@hotmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5bc6abce2f84fa4f1a41bef6adc342c8850caa7e)
